  'The larger boulder is about four and a half feet high with a large flying bird on its flattest face. The smaller one, with a smaller bird and a headless second one above it, was kept for years at the University of North Dakota and came back in 1965. Both now stand in a shelter behind iron bars, so you look through the bars. Picnic shelters and a playground are on the grounds.',
