  'The ranch Theodore Roosevelt set up in 1884 on the Little Missouri River, 35 miles north of Medora, and called his home ranch. Two Maine woodsmen, Bill Sewall and Wilmot Dow, built a log house of eight rooms with a long porch (30 by 60 feet), with a barn, cattle shed, chicken house and blacksmith shop. Roosevelt stopped using it after 1890 and sold it in 1898. A local stockman said that by 1901 nothing was left but a couple of half-rotted foundations.',
